{"type":"work_unit","id":"WORK-6ds59btb76","title":"Diff viewer Dioxus component","slug":"diff-viewer-component","created":"2026-09-14","kind":"preplanned","source":"ad-hoc","state":"backlog","maturity":{"status":"DREAMED"},"workDiscipline":"coding","workVariety":"greenfield","importance":"high","urgency":"med","priority":"high","epic_id":"EPIC-77znwqj94w","problem_context":"- Dioxus apps need a diff viewer they can mount: split or inline views, unchanged lines folded around changes, line numbers, highlighted and clickable lines, titles, and consumer rendering of line content and fold rows.\n- The reference is `src/index.tsx`; the component renders the line diff engine's output rather than diffing on its own.","plan_guidance":"- Every in-scope requirement binds acceptance alongside the criteria.\n- Defaults generally follow react-diff-viewer, per stakeholder steering.\n- Before work-ready, pre-work settles with the Architect the Dioxus forms of fold reset, the content renderer, and the fold-row renderer, captured as candidate architecture that implementation holds to.\n- Palettes, themes, and style overrides belong to the theming work unit; this unit renders markup that theming styles.\n- Risk signals carried from the epic: implementation-complexity and architectural-uncertainty; the stakeholder chose one work unit over a paired split.","status_summary":"Spun out of the port epic with activities and criteria consented. Waits on the line diff engine work unit. Next: collaborative pre-work review, Architect leading with Code Whisperer and Rust Tester, settling the Dioxus forms of fold reset and the two renderers before work-ready.","crAt":"20260915T201549.771Z","upAt":"20260915T201549.771Z"}
