{"type":"work_report","id":"WORK:report-e5srytp0k1","work_unit":"WORK-6ds59btb76","author_skill":"Work Planner","at":"2026-09-15T20:17:00Z","body":"**Commits**\n- `ef948f4`: view, folding, selection, and content requirements drafted DREAMED for this unit's scope.\n- `ad61492`: custom fold rows receive the first hidden line's numbers.\n\n**Clarifications**\n- The reference fold renderer names its arguments start line numbers but passes the line after a middle fold and the last hidden line of a trailing fold; the stakeholder chose the first hidden line, now in the Fold rows requirement.\n\n**Observations**\n- `src/index.tsx:507-515` drops a single trailing unchanged line with no fold row; the folding requirements deliberately do not carry that over, so do not port it from the reference; medium severity for anyone porting line by line.\n- `src/index.tsx:169` hands the click handler the mouse event as well as the line id; the Line number clicks requirement names only the id, and what else a Dioxus handler receives is part of the renderer and handler design pre-work settles.\n\n**For the next worker**\n- The UI group loads in full per the Rust Roundup rule; Appshell Expert and Forms Expert have little bearing on a standalone component and are loaded for completeness, not for guidance to apply.","crAt":"20260915T201645.758Z","upAt":"20260915T201645.758Z"}
